# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
# Task 2250, M-compatibility-promise, 2026-10-29 (panel 230's fallback, its
# condition met by decision 2241): a code computed as the program runs and
# outside 0 to 255 stops the program at the program's own call of `exit`,
# never at a line of `<heroes library>` (through a function value it is the
# library's declaration, the one place such a call has, panel 230's R1),
# where a shell reading only its low
# eight bits once saw 256 as a success (defect 2224). The line before the
# call prints, so the stop is the call's.

function doubled(n: i64) -> i64
    return n * 2

function main()
    print("before")
    exit(code: doubled(128))
